0,Uradhi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uradhi_language,"Urradhi proper is the south-western dialect of the language. The name is composed of urra ""this"" and the proprietive dhi ""having"". The south-eastern dialect of the Wuthathi people, also spelled Wudhadhi, is made of the same elements, with wudha being ""this"". It went extinct in the 1910s. [6]",Uradhi,Australian
